+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Request
+Review how `applyPatch` checks and applies patches and make it conform to RFC 6902, errors included.
+
+## Done
+- Reviewed every operation against RFC 6902 (add, remove, replace, move, copy, test; atomicity; pointer errors).
+- `replace` now overwrites the target in place, so an object member keeps its position (it was removed and re-added, moving it last).
+- Sparse patch arrays (holes) are rejected instead of silently skipped.
+- A `value` of `undefined` is rejected as a missing value (not JSON).
+- Test added in `test/patch.test.ts`; all tests pass.
